## Day 1 Summary

### Key Symbols in Linux Terminal

| Symbol | Meaning                              | Represents          |
|--------|--------------------------------------|---------------------|
| $      | Normal User                          | Limited privileges  |
| #      | Root / Administrator                 | Full privileges     |

### Day 1 Commands Table

| Command        | What It Does                              | Example                  | When to Use                              | Important Notes |
|----------------|-------------------------------------------|--------------------------|------------------------------------------|-----------------|
| --help         | Shows help and usage of any command       | ls --help                | When you forget how a command works      | Very useful for beginners |
| cd             | Change Directory                          | cd Documents             | To move into folders                     | Linux is case-sensitive |
| ls             | List files and folders                    | ls or ls -la             | To see contents of current location      | -la shows hidden files |
| touch          | Create a new empty file                   | touch myfile.txt         | To quickly create files                  | .filename makes hidden file |
| sudo           | Run command with admin rights             | sudo apt update          | When you get Permission Denied           | Use only when needed |
| sudo su        | Switch to full Root user                  | sudo su                  | Need complete admin access               | Always exit after use |
| exit           | Leave root or current session             | exit                     | After finishing admin tasks              | - |
| apt update     | Update the package list                   | sudo apt update          | Before installing any software           | Always run this first |

### Important Concepts

| Topic                        | Details |
|-----------------------------|---------|
| Case Sensitivity            | Linux is case-sensitive. "Desktop" and "desktop" are different. |
| Permission Denied           | Happens when you are a normal user and try admin tasks. Use sudo. |
| Home Directory              | 70% of all work is done here. Use cd ~ to go to Home. |
| File & Folder Colors        | Different colors show files vs folders (Blue = folder). |
| File Permissions            | Example: drwxr-xr-x tells who can read, write or execute. |

### Recommended Practice Steps (Day 1)

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| 1    | Check current location |
| 2    | List all files and folders |
| 3    | Go to Home directory |
| 4    | Create a new file |
| 5    | List files again to verify |
| 6    | Go back one folder |
| 7    | Update system packages |
| 8    | Exit root if used |

